The legal texts come from Kenya Law (National Council for Law Reporting, on the Laws.Africa Peachjam platform):

  Kenya Law, https://new.kenyalaw.org, point-in-time versions of each act, read from archived copies of its
  pages on the Internet Archive (https://web.archive.org), retrieved 2026-10-28.

Licence and terms, as Kenya Law states them: Kenya Law terms of use s. 9 (https://kenyalaw.org/terms-of-use/): raw, unannotated source documents CC BY-NC 4.0 crediting NCLR; automated scraping, bulk extraction, commercial redistribution and AI training need an explicit Licensing Agreement from NCLR.
CC BY-NC 4.0: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/legalcode

Attribution:

  Source: Kenya Law, the National Council for Law Reporting (https://kenyalaw.org). Raw source documents are made available under the Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0 International licence (CC BY-NC 4.0); NCLR's terms of use require an explicit Licensing Agreement for automated extraction and commercial redistribution.

The texts may be used only for non-commercial purposes. This repository is private; whether and how it
may be published is the owner's decision under these terms.

Changes made by Lexifina: each version was converted to one Markdown file per provision, one paragraph per
line; spacing, quotes and dashes were normalised; editorial notes, Part and Chapter headings were left out;
and the versions were arranged as git commits credited to the laws Kenya Law names for each change.
The wording of the law was not changed. Neither Kenya Law nor Laws.Africa endorses this repository.

Lexifina's own contributions (the arrangement of the history, the commit messages, the tables and the
tools) are dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal:
https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode
